 "notes": "Stretch 1, pp. 123-124 (PDF 287-288). Start p. 123 row 1 'tua Rā em uben - f' under the top rule; end p. 124 row 9 'ta' (the earth). Plate heading 'PLATE XIX.' after p. 123 row 2; rows 1-2 of p. 123 = Plate XVIII, all later words Plate XIX. No footnotes, no square brackets in any hieroglyph line (brackets only in Budge's transliteration '[k]' and English). Line numerals: '1.' p.123 row 1 before ṭua; '2.' p.123 row 2 before Rā (second-to-last group); '3.' p.123 row 4 inside χu (after G25 Aa1); '4.' p.123 row 5 inside āṭtet (before X1 X1 + boat); '5.' p.123 row 7 inside ḥennu-nek (after O4 N35); '6.' p.123 row 8 before ḥetep; '7.' p.124 row 2 before Tem; '8.' p.124 row 3 before neteru; '9.' p.124 row 5 inside mer Ṭes Ṭes (before the final N36); '10.' p.124 row 7 before nefer; '11.' p.124 row 9 inside ṭua-k (before V31). Last numeral on p. 124 is 11. Overlines (rubric) only on p.123 rows 1-2: (a) over '1.'/ṭua; (b) from em through uben-f to em (NOT over Rā, which stands between overlines a and b); χut not overlined; (c) from er through χeper, ḥetep-f, em to row end; row 2: one overline over ānχ t'eṭ àn (Àusàr onward not overlined). No overlines on p. 124. Recurrent twisted-cord sign (V28 shape) appears in net'em, seku, ḥept-tu, seḥeq, sek-nes — coded V28 throughout as printed. Two different sektet boat dets: p.123 boat with cabin (P3 approx), p.124 boat with sail (P2 approx)."
